                "args": {
                  "ticket_id": "63",
                  "body": "Hello,\n\nThank you for reaching out about the 429 errors you're experiencing with your API requests.\n\n**What the 429 error means:**\nA 429 response indicates that you have exceeded the API rate limit for your API key.\n\n**Our API rate limits:**\nOur API has a rate limit of 100 requests per minute per key. When you exceed this limit, you'll receive 429 error responses.\n\n**How to resolve this:**\nTo resolve the 429 errors, you need to:\n\n1. **Back off** - Stop making requests temporarily when you receive a 429 response\n2. **Retry with exponential delay** - Implement a retry mechanism that waits progressively longer between retry attempts (for example: wait 1 second, then 2 seconds, then 4 seconds, etc.)\n3. **Reduce your request rate** - Ensure your application doesn't exceed 100 requests per minute per API key\n\n**Important note:**\nThere is no higher tier available that raises this rate limit, so you'll need to work within the 100 requests per minute constraint.\n\nIf you need to make more requests, consider spreading them out over time or batching operations where possible to stay within the rate limit.\n\nPlease let me know if you need any clarification on implementing the retry logic or have questions about optimizing your API usage.\n\nBest regards"
                },
